====================================================================
RDGMFEQ OPERATOR LINKING FRAMEWORK
====================================================================

We define three layers:

    SID-layer:   structural + interaction + dynamical modes
    PED-layer:   power + evaluation + dynamics flux
    RDG-layer:   primitive relational operators

The links between them are NOT implicit; they are explicit morphisms.

====================================================================
TYPE DEFINITIONS
====================================================================

TYPE Link =
    SID_to_PED
    PED_to_RDG
    RDG_to_SID
    RDG_Compose
    Flux_Couple

TYPE State =
    GeometricState
    MetricState
    PhaseState
    ProjectiveState
    ConicState
    EquilibriumState

TYPE Flux =
    PowerFlux
    EvalFlux
    DynFlux

TYPE Morphism =
    f : A -> B

====================================================================
CORE LINKING PRINCIPLES
====================================================================

1. SID_to_PED:
   Structure, Interaction, Dynamics each induce a corresponding
   Power/Evaluation/Dynamics flux channel.

   Morphisms:
       S -> PowerFlux
       I -> EvalFlux
       D -> DynFlux

2. PED_to_RDG:
   Flux channels activate specific RDG operators.

   Morphisms:
       PowerFlux -> {IsoOp, LinMap}
       EvalFlux  -> {PhaseOp, ProjExtract, AlignOp}
       DynFlux   -> {ConicDyn, MomentEq}

3. RDG_to_SID:
   The result of an RDG operator modifies the SID mode of the state.

   Morphisms:
       IsoOp       -> Structure update
       AlignOp     -> Interaction update
       ConicDyn    -> Dynamics update
       MomentEq    -> Interaction update
       PhaseOp     -> Structure update (phase embedding)
       LinMap      -> Structure update (scale embedding)
       ProjExtract -> Structure update (direction embedding)

4. RDG_Compose:
   RDG operators compose sequentially into relational pipelines.

   Composition rule:
       RDG_i ∘ RDG_j : State -> State

5. Flux_Couple:
   Flux channels couple when multiple SID modes are active.

   Example:
       Interaction + Dynamics ->
           EvalFlux + DynFlux ->
               AlignOp + ConicDyn (coupled)

