====================================================================
PIPELINE EXAMPLE (FULL CHAIN)
====================================================================

Given a geometric state G:

1. SID mode selects flux:
       SID(G) -> Flux(G)

2. Flux activates RDG operator:
       Flux(G) -> RDG_op

3. RDG operator transforms state:
       RDG_op(G) -> G'

4. G' updates SID mode:
       G' -> SID(G')

5. SID(G') selects next flux, continuing pipeline.

This defines a closed relational geometry loop:
       G -> SID -> PED -> RDG -> G'

====================================================================
RDGMFEQ EXECUTION SEMANTICS
====================================================================
1. BASE OBJECTS
====================================================================

Channel multiplicity • Lifted state transforms • Execution & coupling rules

TYPE SID = {S, I, D}              // Structure, Interaction, Dynamics
TYPE PED = {P, E, Dn}            // Power, Evaluation, Dynamics (flux)
TYPE RDG_Op                      // primitive relational operator
TYPE State                       // geometric / relational state

We now allow MULTI-CHANNEL activation:

SID_Set ⊆ {S, I, D}
PED_Set ⊆ {P, E, Dn}
RDG_Set ⊆ {IsoOp, PhaseOp, AlignOp, SimOp, LinMap, ConicDyn, MomentEq, ProjExtract}

====================================================================
2. CHANNEL MULTIPLICITY
====================================================================

We define channel activation maps:

SID_to_PED : SID_Set -> PED_Set
PED_to_RDG : PED_Set -> RDG_Set

RULE 2.1 (SID_to_PED multiplicity):
    If SID_Set = {S}       then PED_Set ⊇ {P}
    If SID_Set = {I}       then PED_Set ⊇ {E}
    If SID_Set = {D}       then PED_Set ⊇ {Dn}
    If SID_Set = {S,I}     then PED_Set ⊇ {P,E}
    If SID_Set = {S,D}     then PED_Set ⊇ {P,Dn}
    If SID_Set = {I,D}     then PED_Set ⊇ {E,Dn}
    If SID_Set = {S,I,D}   then PED_Set ⊇ {P,E,Dn}

RULE 2.2 (PED_to_RDG multiplicity):
    P   activates {IsoOp, LinMap, SimOp}
    E   activates {PhaseOp, ProjExtract, AlignOp, SimOp, MomentEq}
    Dn  activates {ConicDyn, MomentEq}

Thus, multiple SID modes induce multiple PED channels,
which in turn activate a SET of RDG operators.

====================================================================
3. LIFTED STATE TRANSFORMATIONS
====================================================================

We now lift RDG operators from single-state maps to
multi-channel, multi-operator transformations.

BASE (non-lifted):
    RDG_Op : State -> State

LIFTED:
    RDG_Lift : (State, RDG_Set) -> State'

Definition:
    RDG_Lift(State, RDG_Set) =
        fold(Compose, State, RDG_Set)

where:
    Compose(State, Op) = Op(State)
    fold is left-associative composition over RDG_Set
    (ordering rules defined below).

SID_Lift : (State, SID_Set) -> (State', PED_Set, RDG_Set)

Definition:
    SID_Lift(State, SID_Set) =
        let PED_Set = SID_to_PED(SID_Set)
        let RDG_Set = PED_to_RDG(PED_Set)
        let State'  = RDG_Lift(State, RDG_Set)
        in (State', PED_Set, RDG_Set)

Thus, SID_Set determines PED_Set and RDG_Set, and the lifted
RDG_Lift applies all activated operators to the state.

====================================================================
4. EXECUTION RULES
====================================================================

We define an EXECUTION STEP as:

ExecStep : State -> State'

ExecStep(State) =
    1. Determine active SID_Set(State)
    2. Compute (State', PED_Set, RDG_Set) = SID_Lift(State, SID_Set)
    3. Return State'

We now specify SID_Set(State):

SID_Set(State) is determined by:
    • Structural flags (S-active)
    • Interaction flags (I-active)
    • Dynamical flags (D-active)

For this formalization, we treat SID_Set(State) as given
by the instrument context (e.g., “ellipsograph” implies D-active).

====================================================================
5. COUPLING RULES (MULTI-CHANNEL)
====================================================================

Coupling occurs when multiple PED channels are active simultaneously.

We define a COUPLING GRAPH:

Couple : PED_Set -> RDG_Set_coupled

RULE 5.1 (basic coupling):
    If PED_Set = {P,E}:
        RDG_Set_coupled ⊆ {SimOp, AlignOp, PhaseOp, IsoOp, LinMap}
    If PED_Set = {P,Dn}:
        RDG_Set_coupled ⊆ {ConicDyn, MomentEq, IsoOp, LinMap}
    If PED_Set = {E,Dn}:
        RDG_Set_coupled ⊆ {ConicDyn, MomentEq, AlignOp, PhaseOp}
    If PED_Set = {P,E,Dn}:
        RDG_Set_coupled = union of all above

RULE 5.2 (priority ordering):
    For RDG_Lift, we impose an operator order:

    1. IsoOp, LinMap, SimOp      (structural normalization)
    2. AlignOp, PhaseOp, ProjExtract (evaluation / alignment)
    3. MomentEq, ConicDyn        (equilibrium / motion)

Thus:
    RDG_Set_effective = sort(RDG_Set ∪ RDG_Set_coupled, by priority)

RDG_Lift(State, RDG_Set_effective) applies operators in this order.

====================================================================
6. EXECUTION LOOP (LIFTED, COUPLED)
====================================================================

Given initial State_0:

Loop:
    State_{n+1} = ExecStep(State_n)

ExecStep(State_n):
    1. SID_Set_n = SID_Set(State_n)
    2. PED_Set_n = SID_to_PED(SID_Set_n)
    3. RDG_Set_n = PED_to_RDG(PED_Set_n)
    4. RDG_Set_coupled_n = Couple(PED_Set_n)
    5. RDG_Set_effective_n = sort(RDG_Set_n ∪ RDG_Set_coupled_n)
    6. State_{n+1} = RDG_Lift(State_n, RDG_Set_effective_n)

This defines the EXECUTION and COUPLING semantics without
changing the interpretation of SID/PED/RDG—only lifting and
multiplicity resolution.

====================================================================
7. INSTRUMENT-SPECIFIC LIFTED EXAMPLES (SKETCH)
====================================================================

VERNIER (Interaction-dominant):
    SID_Set = {I}
    PED_Set = {E}
    RDG_Set = {AlignOp}
    RDG_Set_effective = {AlignOp}
    RDG_Lift = AlignOp(State)

ELLIPSOGRAPH (Dynamics-dominant):
    SID_Set = {D}
    PED_Set = {Dn}
    RDG_Set = {ConicDyn}
    RDG_Set_effective = {ConicDyn}
    RDG_Lift = ConicDyn(State)

SECTOR (Structure+Interaction):
    SID_Set = {S,I}
    PED_Set = {P,E}
    RDG_Set = {IsoOp, LinMap, SimOp, PhaseOp, AlignOp}
    RDG_Set_coupled ⊆ {SimOp, AlignOp, PhaseOp}
    RDG_Set_effective ordered:
        [IsoOp, LinMap, SimOp, AlignOp, PhaseOp]
    RDG_Lift applies full proportional pipeline.

====================================================================
SUMMARY
====================================================================

The links between equations are explicit morphisms:

    SID_to_PED:   mode → flux
    PED_to_RDG:   flux → operator
    RDG_to_SID:   operator → mode update
    RDG_Compose:  operator chaining
    Flux_Couple:  multi‑mode coupling


